# A default interval Interval<T, 1> [xl, xu] as a state of the round-up interval
# (docs/developer/design/upward.md, "Conversions"): (xu, -xl), and the default empty set
# (+inf, -inf) as (NaN, NaN). Exact, in every rounding mode: the same set, the signs of zero bounds
# aside. Requires the rounding mode upward set by kairn::upward::Scope and the options of
# docs/concepts/upward.md (GCC and Clang -frounding-math, MSVC /fp:strict).
kernel:        upward_from_interval_1
rounding:      upward
input:         stored xl
input:         stored xu
output:        pair z = zu zn
requires:      interval xl xu
ensures:       same_set zu zn from=xl,xu
min_precision: 1
source:        the upper bound and the negated lower bound, the empty set after a test (the listing of the round-up interval)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_only:     yes
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeUpwardExact.v upward_from_interval_1_correct
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   both lanes are selected after a test of the default empty set; same_set states what comes out for every canonical default interval

e  = eq(xl, const inf)                                         # its empty set
nl = neg(xl)
zu = select(e, const nan, xu) | zn = select(e, const nan, nl)  # (xu, -xl): a make
